A||||12||Carrolles||MSD Ignition results ???||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||06-05-2001||09:22 AM||||Does anyone have real results of installing an MSD ignition system?  G-tech or Dyno results would be great.<P>When I finally do mine I'll run before and after G-tech averages and post the results.  I'm just wondering if it is worth the money.<P>I'm talking about the MSD 6AL (I think that's the recommended one) and the recommended coil.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||06-05-2001||04:32 PM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||06-05-2001||05:10 PM||||You may not be able to measure a difference with a G-tech because it would be too small. Maybe with a Dyno. But you should feel the engine stronger specially at high RPM. Also idle could be smoother. That's what I got with my Jacobs and wires. To me a MSD is a worthwhile investment if you want to squeeze the max out of your ignition system.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||06-05-2001||05:15 PM||||I have a question, what MSD system are you guys talking about? Are you just talking about the MSD coil, and module, or the flow-blown ignition system box? How much do these things cost? Where can I get it? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||06-05-2001||07:53 PM||||I put an MSD 6A on my GT.<BR>Don't have any dyno or G-yech data but I can tell you that it does actually make a difference. The throttle is much more responsive, down right sensitive as a matter<BR>of fact, and it starts better and even helps the hunting idle problem. It's worth the price of addmission!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000005||L.I. Fieros||06-05-2001||11:51 PM||||Hey, I've got an MSD 6AL on my 2.8 motor.  Been running it for about a year and a half now.  Originally I had some cheap-o ignition wires so I couldn't feel any difference.  The wires used to get so hot that you couldn't even touch them.  About 8 months ago, though, I put on a set of MSD Superconductor 8.5 mm. wires and then began to see the results.  The G-Tech, which I use as a baseline, showed a consistent 1 hp. increase after I installed the wires.  This is not really a big deal.  However, my gas mileage (around town) went from about 19 mpg. to 22.5 mpg.  That's where the real story is.  I just hope it keeps up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>See ya,<BR>Dave<BR>LIFE<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||BV MotorSports||06-06-2001||01:22 AM||||Hey you guys are running the 93-95 Camaro/ Firebird MSD wiring harness right?<BR>Coil is the same and wiring is the same. I used a MSD 6AL, Super coil and F-Body wiring harness out of my buddies wrecked 95 Camaro Z28.<BR>Swapped right on to my 87 GT. No cutting or splicing.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000007||dr fritz||06-08-2001||12:08 AM||||For those of you that have MSD ignition or some sort of equivalent.  What was the cost and have they been reliable?  I have heard that back in the day these aftermarket ignitions would easily turn to smoke... <BR>   a) leaving you stranded<P>   b) leaving your wallet empty<P> any and all info is much appreciated<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cozmo||06-08-2001||08:05 AM||||I just put the MSD 8226 GM blaster coil on, soon the 6AL module.  So far, all I notice is it seems to rev more freely and idle smoother. (ass-o-meter only, no dyno stuff...)<BR>It is a pretty red color tho... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><B>C02M0</B>  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||WampusCat||06-08-2001||08:13 AM||||My 92 Toyota 3.0 pickup has a Jacobs mileage master computer and coil.  The installation kept the original coil so it's easy to switch back and forth by moving the coil wire.  I can tell a definite improvement in smoothness and higher rpm power with the Jacobs system.  I've been using it for about 60k miles now with no problems.  The previous owner put it on the truck and threw it in with the deal so I don't know what it cost new.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dave Gunsul||06-08-2001||11:25 AM||||Dr Fritz, my MSD 6A cost $129.99 from Jegs high performance and hasn't left me stranded<BR>once. See my above post for opinions.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000011||Slammed Fiero||06-08-2001||02:28 PM||||Grassroots motorsports got 3 rear wheel Hp with an MSD unit and blaster coil on a honda. Not earth shattering. I have read a lot on ignition systems , they just make sure that the spark is there when it's needed..like int he upper RPM ranges. I believe Hot Rod TV had soemthing on this a while back<P>Jaccobs makes a nice unit that does claim to ad HP. I only know one guy who has used it on a fiero and he said he did notice quite a difference. expensive though.<P>I wonder what sort of power I may be loosing by running the original wires (haha) ..Better get new ones this weekend...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> there goes some more money<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
